#{[{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186419683 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186129130 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "61bd0b4f-165c-5f31-b4ec-e0eff7e758e1" :knowledge-point/title "Finding the Matrix of a Linear Transformation Relative to a Basis Using a Change-of-Coordinates Matrix"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "3cd07fe6-6fc8-5bf5-a02a-2d9be90b12af" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}7 & 6 \\\\ -14 & -10\\end{aligned}]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186419666} {:answer/id #uuid "5e5ddfaa-301e-59f4-a460-764955ae24fe" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}10 & 6 \\\\ -14 & -7\\end{aligned}]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186419668} {:answer/id #uuid "6431b86f-886e-5d1c-a26b-505391b5eaa1" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}10 & -6 \\\\ 14 & 9\\end{aligned}]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186419669} {:answer/id #uuid "9029cfa0-da2b-5680-a6e9-bd10f503ed2f" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}6 & 10 \\\\ -14 & -7\\end{aligned}]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186419672} {:answer/id #uuid "b7bd80ae-8e71-5474-9567-c47f73ef5af4" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}10 & -7 \\\\ -14 & 6\\end{aligned}]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186419673}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "5e5ddfaa-301e-59f4-a460-764955ae24fe" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}10 & 6 \\\\ -14 & -7\\end{aligned}]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186419668} :answer-field/id #uuid "80639a3b-2c96-57ee-bd01-981e0851478b" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186419682}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "426fab7e-1490-581a-8c87-fe143e595ca4" :question/math-academy-id "q-140453" :question/problem "$$\n[T]_{B}=[\\begin{aligned}2 & -3 \\\\ 4 & 1\\end{aligned}],\\,{P}_{B\\to C}=[\\begin{aligned}1 & -1 \\\\ -2 & 1\\end{aligned}]\n$$\n\nConsider the matrix $[T]_{B}$ of a linear transformation $T$ with respect to the basis $B$ and the change-of-coordinates matrix ${P}_{B\\to C}$ shown above. Find the matrix of $T$ relative to the basis $C.$" :question/worked-solution "The connection between the matrices of our linear transformation $T$ relative to the bases $B$ and $C$ is given by the following diagram:\n\n![](images/1b/1b81504d6fdcabee0e1f586fef3dd2af5a57a8411ba4d22429e00e09b171a4d1.png)\n\n \n\nHere, moving along an arrow means pre-multiplying by the corresponding matrix. Algebraically, we can write this as\n\n$$\n[T]_{C}={P}_{B\\to C}\\cdot [T]_{B}\\cdot {P}_{B\\to C}^{-1}\\,,\n$$\n\nwhere ${P}_{B\\to C}$ is the change-of-coordinates matrix from $B$ to $C.$\n\nOur goal is to compute $[T]_{C}.$ First, we compute the inverse of ${P}_{B\\to C}:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{P}_{B\\to C}^{-1} & ={[\\begin{aligned}1 & -1 \\\\ -2 & 1\\end{aligned}]}^{-1} \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{1\\cdot 1-(-2)\\cdot (-1)}[\\begin{aligned}1 & 1 \\\\ 2 & 1\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}-1 & -1 \\\\ -2 & -1\\end{aligned}]\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, we can compute the matrix of $T$ relative to the basis $C:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}[T]_{C} & ={P}_{B\\to C}\\cdot [T]_{B}\\cdot {P}_{B\\to C}^{-1} \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}1 & -1 \\\\ -2 & 1\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}2 & -3 \\\\ 4 & 1\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}-1 & -1 \\\\ -2 & -1\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}-2 & -4 \\\\ 0 & 7\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}-1 & -1 \\\\ -2 & -1\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}10 & 6 \\\\ -14 & -7\\end{aligned}]\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186129630 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186129130 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "61bd0b4f-165c-5f31-b4ec-e0eff7e758e1" :knowledge-point/title "Finding the Matrix of a Linear Transformation Relative to a Basis Using a Change-of-Coordinates Matrix"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "b0dcc57b-b70d-5099-8655-1c525b6e5b7a" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\begin{bmatrix}-2 & 4 \\\\ 2 & -5\\end{bmatrix}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186127262} {:answer/id #uuid "d3a8c213-e37c-5cae-a4a0-9928b2b5de18" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\begin{bmatrix}1 & -1 \\\\ 1 & -2\\end{bmatrix}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186127263} {:answer/id #uuid "db7f8e7c-701f-5122-ac01-625e0e9c905d" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\begin{bmatrix}1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & -5\\end{bmatrix}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186127264} {:answer/id #uuid "3343d4eb-e38d-561c-81a6-5e7c140fd645" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\begin{bmatrix}1 & -5 \\\\ 2 & -8\\end{bmatrix}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186127265} {:answer/id #uuid "6b977d7f-c5f1-5444-a63d-5ba017027f85" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\begin{bmatrix}0 & -2 \\\\ -1 & 3\\end{bmatrix}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186127266}] :answer-field/id #uuid "3aa05285-18b6-579f-8c04-dbac65b8b645" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186127261} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "194c5392-aa53-5440-94cc-4abb77800895" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & -5\\end{aligned}]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186392174} {:answer/id #uuid "691927ec-b78a-5e40-b1ee-2622d3ca2016" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}1 & -5 \\\\ 2 & -8\\end{aligned}]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186392175} {:answer/id #uuid "d1b8253f-af1f-5496-b874-d6c428e325fa" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}0 & -2 \\\\ -1 & 3\\end{aligned}]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186392176} {:answer/id #uuid "6826e8b7-4210-5379-a15a-9fb110ae599d" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}1 & -1 \\\\ 1 & -2\\end{aligned}]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186392177} {:answer/id #uuid "a0c0f03c-84bf-55b5-8770-d4b6ac71bcb4" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}-2 & 4 \\\\ 2 & -5\\end{aligned}]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186392178}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "a0c0f03c-84bf-55b5-8770-d4b6ac71bcb4" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}-2 & 4 \\\\ 2 & -5\\end{aligned}]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186392178} :answer-field/id #uuid "26a5ee64-c45e-5ae2-97b9-195b22b8e981" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186392173}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "ba13dd29-8b1d-5a17-aa9e-1e011399048f" :question/math-academy-id "q-38096" :question/problem "$$\n[T]_{B}=[\\begin{aligned}1 & -5 \\\\ 2 & -8\\end{aligned}],\\,{P}_{B\\to C}=[\\begin{aligned}2 & -1 \\\\ 1 & -1\\end{aligned}]\n$$\n\nConsider the matrix $[T]_{B}$ of a linear transformation $T$ with respect to the basis $B$ and the change-of-coordinates matrix ${P}_{B\\to C}$ shown above. Find the matrix of $T$ relative to the basis $C.$" :question/worked-solution "The connection between the matrices of our linear transformation $T$ relative to the bases $B$ and $C$ is given by the following diagram:\n\n![](images/1b/1b81504d6fdcabee0e1f586fef3dd2af5a57a8411ba4d22429e00e09b171a4d1.png)\n\n \n\nHere, moving along an arrow means pre-multiplying by the corresponding matrix. Algebraically, we can write this as\n\n$$\n[T]_{C}={P}_{B\\to C}\\cdot [T]_{B}\\cdot {P}_{B\\to C}^{-1}\\,,\n$$\n\nwhere ${P}_{B\\to C}$ is the change-of-coordinates matrix from $B$ to $C.$\n\nOur goal is to compute $[T]_{C}.$ First, we compute the inverse of ${P}_{B\\to C}:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{P}_{B\\to C}^{-1} & ={[\\begin{aligned}2 & -1 \\\\ 1 & -1\\end{aligned}]}^{-1} \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{2\\cdot (-1)-1\\cdot (-1)}[\\begin{aligned}-1 & 1 \\\\ -1 & 2\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}1 & -1 \\\\ 1 & -2\\end{aligned}]\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, we can compute the matrix of $T$ relative to the basis $C:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}[T]_{C} & ={P}_{B\\to C}\\cdot [T]_{B}\\cdot {P}_{B\\to C}^{-1} \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}2 & -1 \\\\ 1 & -1\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}1 & -5 \\\\ 2 & -8\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}1 & -1 \\\\ 1 & -2\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}0 & -2 \\\\ -1 & 3\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}1 & -1 \\\\ 1 & -2\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}-2 & 4 \\\\ 2 & -5\\end{aligned}]\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186360756 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186129131 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "969220db-a686-511b-b33a-0b4f6ab66b1a" :knowledge-point/title "Finding the Matrix of a Linear Transformation Relative to the Standard Basis"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "2b475445-5cb4-5710-982b-724fa1edd22e" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}-2 & 1 \\\\ -23 & 10\\end{aligned}]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186358141} {:answer/id #uuid "66790505-e184-5aa7-b181-1d0f53118c51" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}2 & -1 \\\\ 23 & -10\\end{aligned}]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186358648} {:answer/id #uuid "81f4c14a-f6f2-5e02-b601-4575f31e25cf" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}-2 & -1 \\\\ 23 & -10\\end{aligned}]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186358888} {:answer/id #uuid "adafbfb4-cdbb-5b64-803a-bfb001366afb" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 \\\\ 4 & 3\\end{aligned}]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186359256} {:answer/id #uuid "c86387e2-3b9d-5570-96f9-1518ba1d80bf" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}-1 & 0 \\\\ -4 & -3\\end{aligned}]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186359514}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "2b475445-5cb4-5710-982b-724fa1edd22e" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}-2 & 1 \\\\ -23 & 10\\end{aligned}]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186358141} :answer-field/id #uuid "5157a8f9-f32d-5e2c-90a2-9716a66d6cb7" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186360122}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "1b879b1b-6896-5c9b-8a36-8fd36dfcc350" :question/math-academy-id "q-97122" :question/problem "$$\nB={[\\begin{aligned}2 \\\\ 5\\end{aligned}],[\\begin{aligned}-1 \\\\ -2\\end{aligned}]},\\,[T]_{B}=[\\begin{aligned}2 & 3 \\\\ 3 & 6\\end{aligned}]\n$$\n\nConsider the basis $B$ of ${R}^{2}$ and the matrix $[T]_{B}$ of a linear transformation $T$ with respect to this basis. Find the matrix of $T$ relative to the standard basis $S.$" :question/worked-solution "The connection between the matrices of our linear transformation $T$ relative to the basis $B$ and standard basis $S$ is given by the following diagram:\n\n![](images/db/dbd020362f950fe8bfb4c592652b9e78a73610fa01a247b0b7ead6f201bf9ea5.png)\n\n \n\nHere, moving along an arrow means pre-multiplying by the corresponding matrix. Algebraically, we can write this as\n\n$$\n[T]_{S}={P}_{B\\to S}\\cdot [T]_{B}\\cdot {P}_{B\\to S}^{-1},\n$$\n\nand the change-of-coordinates matrix from $B$ to $S$ is\n\n$$\n{P}_{B\\to S}=[\\begin{aligned}2 & -1 \\\\ 5 & -2\\end{aligned}].\n$$\n\nFirst, we compute the inverse of ${P}_{B\\to S}:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{P}_{B\\to S}^{-1} & ={[\\begin{aligned}2 & -1 \\\\ 5 & -2\\end{aligned}]}^{-1} \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{(-2)\\cdot 2-(-1)\\cdot 5}[\\begin{aligned}-2 & 1 \\\\ -5 & 2\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}-2 & 1 \\\\ -5 & 2\\end{aligned}].\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, we can compute the matrix of $T$ relative to the standard basis $S:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}[T]_{S} & ={P}_{B\\to S}\\cdot [T]_{B}\\cdot {P}_{B\\to S}^{-1} \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}2 & -1 \\\\ 5 & -2\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}2 & 3 \\\\ 3 & 6\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}-2 & 1 \\\\ -5 & 2\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 \\\\ 4 & 3\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}-2 & 1 \\\\ -5 & 2\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}-2 & 1 \\\\ -23 & 10\\end{aligned}]\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186395256 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186129155 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "86028fae-a119-5194-975d-a6d9fad6faf5" :knowledge-point/title "Finding the Matrix of a Linear Transformation Relative to a Given Basis"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "0dba848e-8a50-579f-aa1a-cc8b6a92a123" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}-4 & -6 \\\\ 1 & 1\\end{aligned}]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186395258} {:answer/id #uuid "8afbc7d4-59ea-5795-91f6-cca9cb7bb68f" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}1 & 3 \\\\ 4 & 11\\end{aligned}]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186395259} {:answer/id #uuid "fd1c3f63-ca96-5f2f-8e18-b4ac0f1ec695" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}-11 & -3 \\\\ -4 & 1\\end{aligned}]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186395260} {:answer/id #uuid "9a6b5e40-d27c-5a06-a89d-52b2c3b456f8" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}20 & -6 \\\\ -7 & 2\\end{aligned}]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186395261} {:answer/id #uuid "8cf7e981-18ce-5505-863b-94d4023785b9" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}-1 & -3 \\\\ -5 & -13\\end{aligned}]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186395262}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "0dba848e-8a50-579f-aa1a-cc8b6a92a123" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}-4 & -6 \\\\ 1 & 1\\end{aligned}]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186395258} :answer-field/id #uuid "39e774e2-138b-5903-abec-0799b97f1fed" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186395257}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045486 :db/ident :question.difficulty/hard} :question/id #uuid "150207d8-196e-5c9f-bf3a-465dd9f4f1f8" :question/math-academy-id "q-97280" :question/problem "$$\nB={[\\begin{aligned}-3 \\\\ -1\\end{aligned}],[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}]},\\,C={[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ 3\\end{aligned}],[\\begin{aligned}2 \\\\ 8\\end{aligned}]},\\,[T]_{B}=[\\begin{aligned}-1 & 0 \\\\ 3 & -2\\end{aligned}]\n$$\n\nConsider the bases $B$ and $C$ of ${R}^{2},$ and the matrix $[T]_{B}$ of a linear transformation $T$ with respect to the basis $B$, shown above. Find the matrix of $T$ relative to the basis $C.$" :question/worked-solution "The connection between the matrices of our linear transformation $T$ relative to the bases $B$ and $C$ is given by the following diagram:\n\n![](images/1b/1b81504d6fdcabee0e1f586fef3dd2af5a57a8411ba4d22429e00e09b171a4d1.png)\n\n \n\nHere, moving along an arrow means pre-multiplying by the corresponding matrix. Algebraically, we can write this as\n\n$$\n[T]_{C}={P}_{B\\to C}\\cdot [T]_{B}\\cdot {P}_{B\\to C}^{-1},\n$$\n\nwhere ${P}_{B\\to C}$ is the change-of-coordinates matrix from $B$ to $C.$\n\nFirst, let's denote the vectors of $B$ and $C$ as ${{b}_{1},{b}_{2}}$ and ${{c}_{1},{c}_{2}}$, respectively.\n\nThe change-of-coordinates matrix from $B$ to $C$ is a matrix whose columns are the coordinates of vectors from $B$ relative to the basis $C.$\n\nHence, we need to find the coordinates of ${b}_{1}$ and ${b}_{2}$ relative to the basis $C.$ To do this, we consider the matrix\n\n$$\nM=[\\begin{aligned}| & | & | & | \\\\ {c}_{1} & {c}_{2} & {b}_{1} & {b}_{2} \\\\ | & | & | & |\\end{aligned}].\n$$\n\nWe reduce $M$ using Gaussian elimination until we get the identity matrix on the left. By doing this, we obtain the required change-of-coordinates matrix on the right.\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}M & =[\\begin{aligned}1 & 2 & -3 & 1 \\\\ 3 & 8 & -1 & 1\\end{aligned}] & {R}_{2} & :={R}_{2}+(-3){R}_{1} \\\\  & ∼[\\begin{aligned}1 & 2 & -3 & 1 \\\\ 0 & 2 & 8 & -2\\end{aligned}] & {R}_{2} & :=\\frac{1}{2}{R}_{2} \\\\  & ∼[\\begin{aligned}1 & 2 & -3 & 1 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 4 & -1\\end{aligned}] & {R}_{1} & :={R}_{1}+(-2){R}_{2} \\\\  & ∼[\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 & -11 & 3 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 4 & -1\\end{aligned}]\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nHence,\n\n$$\n{P}_{B\\to C}=[\\begin{aligned}-11 & 3 \\\\ 4 & -1\\end{aligned}].\n$$\n\nNow, we compute the inverse of ${P}_{B\\to C}:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{P}_{B\\to C}^{-1} & ={[\\begin{aligned}-11 & 3 \\\\ 4 & -1\\end{aligned}]}^{-1} \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{(-1)\\cdot (-11)-4\\cdot 3}[\\begin{aligned}-1 & -3 \\\\ -4 & -11\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}1 & 3 \\\\ 4 & 11\\end{aligned}]\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, we can compute the matrix of $T$ relative to the basis $C:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}[T]_{C} & ={P}_{B\\to C}\\cdot [T]_{B}\\cdot {P}_{B\\to C}^{-1} \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}-11 & 3 \\\\ 4 & -1\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}-1 & 0 \\\\ 3 & -2\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}1 & 3 \\\\ 4 & 11\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}20 & -6 \\\\ -7 & 2\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}1 & 3 \\\\ 4 & 11\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}-4 & -6 \\\\ 1 & 1\\end{aligned}]\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186360778 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186129155 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "86028fae-a119-5194-975d-a6d9fad6faf5" :knowledge-point/title "Finding the Matrix of a Linear Transformation Relative to a Given Basis"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "515e0fc9-c112-5e74-b91b-3ea3532dd376" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}-9 & 7 \\\\ -7 & 6\\end{aligned}]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186358451} {:answer/id #uuid "a2fc8074-c516-5c72-9d38-fc34219514b2" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}9 & -7 \\\\ 3 & -2\\end{aligned}]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186359172} {:answer/id #uuid "d1364a16-2c06-53ff-a9a6-e2611b80cc11" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}-8 & 7 \\\\ 7 & -5\\end{aligned}]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186359582} {:answer/id #uuid "e0062b56-f425-5478-b8b5-1d4bcea7c1e1" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}-6 & 4 \\\\ -8 & 6\\end{aligned}]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186359717} {:answer/id #uuid "efb0e7ec-bdc2-5237-b2c4-a06fbcfdfda5" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}9 & 5 \\\\ 0 & -3\\end{aligned}]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186359888}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "efb0e7ec-bdc2-5237-b2c4-a06fbcfdfda5" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}9 & 5 \\\\ 0 & -3\\end{aligned}]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186359888} :answer-field/id #uuid "7f6b3143-bd7d-5d87-90bd-f6e69c8080aa" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186360207}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045486 :db/ident :question.difficulty/hard} :question/id #uuid "b8a45af8-9088-5825-b97b-d38a2bf5a12a" :question/math-academy-id "q-97283" :question/problem "$$\nB={[\\begin{aligned}10 \\\\ 6\\end{aligned}],[\\begin{aligned}-7 \\\\ -4\\end{aligned}]},\\,C={[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ 2\\end{aligned}],[\\begin{aligned}-1 \\\\ 0\\end{aligned}]},\\,[T]_{B}=[\\begin{aligned}2 & 5 \\\\ 7 & 4\\end{aligned}]\n$$\n\nConsider the bases $B$ and $C$ of ${R}^{2},$ and the matrix $[T]_{B}$ of a linear transformation $T$ with respect to the basis $B$, shown above. Find the matrix of $T$ relative to the basis $C.$" :question/worked-solution "The connection between the matrices of our linear transformation $T$ relative to the bases $B$ and $C$ is given by the following diagram:\n\n![](images/1b/1b81504d6fdcabee0e1f586fef3dd2af5a57a8411ba4d22429e00e09b171a4d1.png)\n\n \n\nHere, moving along an arrow means pre-multiplying by the corresponding matrix. Algebraically, we can write this as\n\n$$\n[T]_{C}={P}_{B\\to C}\\cdot [T]_{B}\\cdot {P}_{B\\to C}^{-1},\n$$\n\nwhere ${P}_{B\\to C}$ is the change-of-coordinates matrix from $B$ to $C.$\n\nFirst, let's denote the vectors of $B$ and $C$ as ${{b}_{1},{b}_{2}}$ and ${{c}_{1},{c}_{2}}$, respectively.\n\nThe change-of-coordinates matrix from $B$ to $C$ is a matrix whose columns are the coordinates of vectors from $B$ relative to the basis $C.$\n\nHence, we need to find the coordinates of ${b}_{1}$ and ${b}_{2}$ relative to the basis $C.$ To do this, we consider the matrix\n\n$$\nM=[\\begin{aligned}| & | & | & | \\\\ {c}_{1} & {c}_{2} & {b}_{1} & {b}_{2} \\\\ | & | & | & |\\end{aligned}].\n$$\n\nWe reduce $M$ using Gaussian elimination until we get the identity matrix on the left. By doing this, we obtain the required change-of-coordinates matrix on the right.\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}M & =[\\begin{aligned}1 & -1 & 10 & -7 \\\\ 2 & 0 & 6 & -4\\end{aligned}] & {R}_{2} & :={R}_{2}+(-2){R}_{1} \\\\  & ∼[\\begin{aligned}1 & -1 & 10 & -7 \\\\ 0 & 2 & -14 & 10\\end{aligned}] & {R}_{2} & :=\\frac{1}{2}{R}_{2} \\\\  & ∼[\\begin{aligned}1 & -1 & 10 & -7 \\\\ 0 & 1 & -7 & 5\\end{aligned}] & {R}_{1} & :={R}_{1}+{R}_{2} \\\\  & ∼[\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 & 3 & -2 \\\\ 0 & 1 & -7 & 5\\end{aligned}]\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nHence,\n\n$$\n{P}_{B\\to C}=[\\begin{aligned}3 & -2 \\\\ -7 & 5\\end{aligned}].\n$$\n\nNow, we compute the inverse of ${P}_{B\\to C}:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{P}_{B\\to C}^{-1} & ={[\\begin{aligned}3 & -2 \\\\ -7 & 5\\end{aligned}]}^{-1} \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{5\\cdot 3-(-7)\\cdot (-2)}[\\begin{aligned}5 & 2 \\\\ 7 & 3\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}5 & 2 \\\\ 7 & 3\\end{aligned}]\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, we can compute the matrix of $T$ relative to the basis $C:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}[T]_{C} & ={P}_{B\\to C}\\cdot [T]_{B}\\cdot {P}_{B\\to C}^{-1} \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}3 & -2 \\\\ -7 & 5\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}2 & 5 \\\\ 7 & 4\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}5 & 2 \\\\ 7 & 3\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}-8 & 7 \\\\ 21 & -15\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}5 & 2 \\\\ 7 & 3\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}9 & 5 \\\\ 0 & -3\\end{aligned}]\\end{aligned}\n$$"}]}
